-- חוק עבודת נשים, התשי"ד-1954 — sections 6, 6א, 7, 7א, 8, 9, 10, 19 and
-- 23: the birth and parenthood period and its length, the absences the law
-- allows (a miscarriage, pregnancy, the months after the period, the
-- parent's hour, fertility treatment, a spouse in reserve duty, the
-- extension of up to a year, check-ups), the provident-fund contributions
-- through the period, that no one is employed in it, the limits on
-- dismissal, on overtime and on night work, that the State is an employer
-- like any other, and that the law takes no better right away. The text is
-- laws/womens-work-law.toml, pinned from the live page of ספר החוקים הפתוח;
-- the corpus holds no copy (MMS-601).
--
-- Why it is here: it sets floors an instrument cannot go below (the
-- Collective Agreements Law §21; §23 here keeps every better right). The
-- agreements and circulars that count "the birth and parenthood period as
-- §6 means it" towards a grant name its length; the takanon's §§1.25.5 and
-- 1.28.2.1 restate §§6, 7 and 9, and where a restatement gives less, the law
-- governs (the root's precedence, l4/lib/precedence.l4).
--
-- Time is counted as the law counts it: the period in weeks, the
-- absences after it in months, the days after an absence in days. An amount
-- or a form the Minister sets by regulation is not pinned; no rule here
-- turns on one.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties

§ `חוק עבודת נשים — תקופת הלידה וההורות, ההיעדרויות, ההפרשות והגבלת הפיטורים`

§§ `6`

-- (א): an employee about to give birth is given the birth and parenthood
-- period by her employer, and is not employed in it (§8 says it again, of
-- the employer who knows). (ב)(1): the period is 26 weeks, of which seven
-- or fewer, as she wishes, before the expected day of the birth; (5): 15
-- weeks, seven or fewer before, for one who worked fewer than twelve months
-- for the same employer or at the same workplace before it, and (1)–(4) do
-- not apply to her.
@ref law:6
GIVEN `months worked for the employer before the period` IS A NUMBER @desc for the same employer or at the same workplace, before she went out on the period
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of the birth and parenthood period` `months worked for the employer before the period` IS
    IF `months worked for the employer before the period` LESS THAN 12 THEN 15 ELSE 26

`most weeks of the birth and parenthood period before the expected birth` MEANS 7

-- (ב)(2): she may shorten the period, to no fewer than 15 weeks (with the
-- extensions of (ב1), (ג) and (ד) she used); (3): once she gives notice,
-- the employer may put her return off by three weeks at most; (4): the
-- Minister may set how the notice is given.
GIVEN `weeks of the extensions she used` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fewest weeks the birth and parenthood period may be shortened to` `weeks of the extensions she used` IS
    15 PLUS `weeks of the extensions she used`

`most weeks the employer may put off a return from a shortened period` MEANS 3

-- (ב1): in hospital for more than two weeks in the period (a stay of 12
-- hours at least, continuous or not), she may extend it by the stay, up to
-- four weeks, or split it (three weeks or more right after the birth, the
-- rest from the stay or its end), on notice the Minister's regulations set.
-- (ג)(1): three weeks more for every further child of one birth, from the
-- second; (2): her spouse may take one stretch of seven days to two weeks
-- of them, in her place and with her consent. (ד): a newborn who stays in,
-- or returns to, hospital for more than two weeks in the period: extend it
-- by the stay, up to twenty weeks, or split it. (ד1) is repealed. (ד3): a
-- newborn recognised in the period as an infant with a complex disability,
-- five weeks more. (ד2): the extensions are cumulative, but those of
-- (ב1)(1), (ד)(1) and (ד3) together not above twenty weeks.
@ref law:6
GIVEN `children born in the birth` IS A NUMBER
      `weeks the mother was in hospital in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `weeks the newborn was in hospital in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `the newborn was recognised as an infant with a complex disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks the birth and parenthood period is extended by` `children born in the birth` `weeks the mother was in hospital in the period` `weeks the newborn was in hospital in the period` `the newborn was recognised as an infant with a complex disability` IS
    3 TIMES max 0 (`children born in the birth` MINUS 1)
    PLUS min 20 `the extensions (ד2) caps`
    WHERE
        `the mother's stay` MEANS
            IF `weeks the mother was in hospital in the period` GREATER THAN 2
            THEN min `weeks the mother was in hospital in the period` 4
            ELSE 0
        `the newborn's stay` MEANS
            IF `weeks the newborn was in hospital in the period` GREATER THAN 2
            THEN min `weeks the newborn was in hospital in the period` 20
            ELSE 0
        `the disability` MEANS
            IF `the newborn was recognised as an infant with a complex disability` THEN 5 ELSE 0
        `the extensions (ד2) caps` MEANS
            `the mother's stay` PLUS `the newborn's stay` PLUS `the disability`

-- (ה): with her consent and a doctor's written approval, the period may be
-- shortened to three weeks after the birth at least, if the child is not
-- alive, she agreed to its adoption, or she is a surrogate mother (the last
-- two on notice the Minister sets). (ו): the Minister may set shorter weeks
-- before the birth for named jobs, up to seven. (ז) is repealed.
GIVEN `the child is not alive, is given for adoption, or she is a surrogate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she consents and a doctor approved in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months worked for the employer before the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fewest weeks after the birth the period may be shortened to under section 6(ה)` `the child is not alive, is given for adoption, or she is a surrogate` `she consents and a doctor approved in writing` `months worked for the employer before the period` IS
    IF `the child is not alive, is given for adoption, or she is a surrogate` AND `she consents and a doctor approved in writing`
    THEN 3
    ELSE `weeks of the birth and parenthood period` `months worked for the employer before the period` MINUS `most weeks of the birth and parenthood period before the expected birth`

-- (ז1): a father whose child is with him and in his sole care, because the
-- mother's disability or illness keeps her from caring for it (a doctor
-- confirms in writing), has the rest of her period, under (ב), (ג) and (ד),
-- from the day those conditions began and while they last; it neither puts
-- off nor shortens hers. (ח): a husband has a partial period after the
-- first six weeks, where his wife waives that part of hers in writing and
-- goes back to work — up to 15 weeks with extensions where he worked
-- fewer than twelve months and she twelve or more; (1ב) seven days in her
-- period, if she waives her last week of maternity pay; the Minister sets
-- the notice. Who takes which weeks is no instrument's question here.
GIVEN `weeks of her period she has not used` IS A NUMBER
      `the child is in his sole care because she cannot care for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of the period a father has under section 6(ז1)` `weeks of her period she has not used` `the child is in his sole care because she cannot care for it` IS
    IF `the child is in his sole care because she cannot care for it` THEN `weeks of her period she has not used` ELSE 0

-- (ט): an absence for the period harms no right that turns on seniority
-- with the employer.
@ref law:6
`the birth and parenthood period harms no right that turns on seniority` MEANS TRUE

#ASSERT `weeks of the birth and parenthood period` 12 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `weeks of the birth and parenthood period` 11 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `weeks the birth and parenthood period is extended by` 2 0 0 FALSE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `weeks the birth and parenthood period is extended by` 1 3 20 TRUE EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `weeks the birth and parenthood period is extended by` 1 2 0 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `fewest weeks after the birth the period may be shortened to under section 6(ה)` TRUE TRUE 24 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `fewest weeks the birth and parenthood period may be shortened to` 3 EQUALS 18

§§ `6א`

-- Repealed; the takanon's §1.25.5 still lists it among its sources.
@ref law:6א
`section 6א of the Women's Work Law is in force` MEANS FALSE

§§ `7`

-- (א): after a miscarriage she may be absent a week, and longer where a
-- doctor confirms her health needs it, as long as he sets, up to six
-- weeks. (ב): it is an absence for illness.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `weeks a doctor set` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 where no doctor confirmed a longer absence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of absence after a miscarriage under the Women's Work Law` `weeks a doctor set` IS
    max 1 (min `weeks a doctor set` 6)

`an absence after a miscarriage is an absence for illness under the Women's Work Law` MEANS TRUE

-- (ג)(1): in pregnancy, as far as a doctor confirms in writing her
-- condition needs it — an absence for illness, unless the
-- pregnancy-protection benefit or another law, agreement or contract pays
-- for it; it harms no right that turns on seniority. (1א), (1ב): where a
-- doctor confirms on the form the regulations set that the work endangers
-- her or the foetus, or keeps her from it, unpaid leave unless the employer
-- finds her suitable other work, seniority unharmed. (1ג): from the end of
-- the period to six months from the birth, while nursing, where section 1
-- forbade employing her because of it and no other work was found, unpaid
-- leave without seniority.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `days a doctor confirmed in writing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of absence in pregnancy under section 7(ג)(1)` `days a doctor confirmed in writing` IS
    `days a doctor confirmed in writing`

`an absence in pregnancy on a doctor's word harms no right that turns on seniority` MEANS TRUE

-- (ג)(2): from the end of the period to six months after it, as far as a
-- doctor confirms her condition after the birth needs it — an absence for
-- illness.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `months a doctor confirmed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months of absence after the period on a doctor's word under the Women's Work Law` `months a doctor confirmed` IS
    min `months a doctor confirmed` 6

-- (ג)(3): from the end of the period to four months after it, an hour a
-- day — the parent's hour — if she works a full position as customary at
-- her workplace, or at least 174 hours a month, whichever is lower; on top
-- of the breaks of the Hours of Work and Rest Law, and not deducted from
-- her pay. A father in such a position may take it alone or by turns with
-- her, on §7ב's conditions (not pinned), the two together no more than she
-- alone would have.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `hours a month she works` IS A NUMBER
      `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `works the position the parent's hour asks` `hours a month she works` `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` IF
    `hours a month she works` AT LEAST min `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` 174

GIVEN `months since the period ended` IS A NUMBER
      `works the position it asks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `minutes a day of the parent's hour under the Women's Work Law` `months since the period ended` `works the position it asks` IS
    IF `works the position it asks` AND `months since the period ended` AT LEAST 0 AND `months since the period ended` LESS THAN `months after the period the parent's hour lasts`
    THEN 60
    ELSE 0

`months after the period the parent's hour lasts` MEANS 4

`the parent's hour is deducted from pay` MEANS FALSE

-- (ג)(4): in fertility treatment, IVF included, as far as the treating
-- doctor confirms in writing and with notice to the employer in advance —
-- an absence for illness; part days may be counted, up to 40 hours a year
-- in a full position as customary, or its share for a part position (her
-- monthly hours over a full position's, or 182, whichever is lower), and
-- they are paid sick pay from the first day; (ג1): so for an employee
-- (a man) in fertility treatment.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `hours a month she works` IS A NUMBER
      `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of a position under section 7 of the Women's Work Law` `hours a month she works` `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` IS
    min 1 (`hours a month she works` DIVIDED BY min `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` 182)

GIVEN `hours a month she works` IS A NUMBER
      `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours of part days of fertility absence a year under section 7(ג)(4)` `hours a month she works` `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` IS
    40 TIMES `the share of a position under section 7 of the Women's Work Law` `hours a month she works` `hours a month of a full position at her workplace`

`a fertility absence is an absence for illness under the Women's Work Law` MEANS TRUE

-- (ג)(5): in a shelter for battered women, up to six months in twelve,
-- after six months with the employer — unpaid leave. (ג)(6): while her
-- spouse serves five or more consecutive days of reserve duty, an hour a
-- day from its first day, if she has a child under 13 with her, works a
-- full position, and gave notice with proof of the service; not on a day
-- she takes the parent's hour (only the rest up to an hour); so for a man
-- whose spouse serves; a security body may suspend it for a week at a time
-- by a reasoned decision; on top of the breaks, and not deducted from pay.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `consecutive days of the spouse's reserve duty` IS A NUMBER
      `age of the youngest child with her` IS A NUMBER
      `works a full position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `gave notice with proof of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `minutes of a parent's hour she takes that day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `minutes a day of absence while the spouse serves in reserve duty` `consecutive days of the spouse's reserve duty` `age of the youngest child with her` `works a full position` `gave notice with proof of the service` `minutes of a parent's hour she takes that day` IS
    IF     `consecutive days of the spouse's reserve duty` AT LEAST 5
       AND `age of the youngest child with her` LESS THAN 13
       AND `works a full position`
       AND `gave notice with proof of the service`
    THEN max 0 (60 MINUS `minutes of a parent's hour she takes that day`)
    ELSE 0

-- (ג2): a man may be absent while his spouse, in hospital, split her
-- period under §6(ב1)(2) (up to four weeks), or while a child born to him
-- is in his sole custody (the rest of the mother's period) — unpaid leave,
-- seniority unharmed; his return may be put off two weeks at most. (ג3):
-- up to five days from the day after his spouse gives birth, the first
-- three as annual leave (unpaid if he has none), the other two as sick
-- days. (ג4): with a year's work, while the newborn is in hospital for more
-- than two weeks, up to 20 days, on his sick days or annual leave.
@ref law:7
`days a spouse may be absent after the birth under section 7(ג3)` MEANS 5

`of them, days as annual leave` MEANS 3

-- (ד)(1): from the end of the period she may be absent a quarter of the
-- months she worked for the same employer or at the same workplace, not
-- past twelve months from the birth; a part of a month is not counted; the
-- weeks by which the period she took exceeded fifteen (with extensions) are
-- deducted. (2): unpaid leave, not counted for seniority. (3): if she
-- reports back, or says she wants to, before the end, her return may be put
-- off four weeks at most. (ד1): so for a man whose spouse worked six
-- consecutive months before, or whose child is in his sole custody or care;
-- (ד2): one spouse's absence excludes the other's but for its rest.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `months worked for the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `months from the birth to the end of the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months of absence after the period under section 7(ד)(1) before the deduction` `months worked for the employer` `months from the birth to the end of the period` IS
    min (TRUNC (`months worked for the employer` DIVIDED BY 4) 0)
        (max 0 (12 MINUS `months from the birth to the end of the period`))

GIVEN `weeks of the period she took` IS A NUMBER
      `weeks of the extensions she used` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks deducted from the absence under section 7(ד)(1)` `weeks of the period she took` `weeks of the extensions she used` IS
    max 0 (`weeks of the period she took` MINUS (15 PLUS `weeks of the extensions she used`))

`the absence after the period under section 7(ד) counts for seniority` MEANS FALSE

`weeks the employer may put off a return from the absence under section 7(ד)` MEANS 4

-- (ה)(1): she may be absent, without deduction from pay, for medical
-- supervision in pregnancy and the routine tests by a gynaecologist or at
-- an approved mother-and-child station; (2): up to 40 hours over the
-- pregnancy in a full position as customary, or its share for a part
-- position (her monthly hours over a full position's, or 182, whichever is
-- lower); (3): the regulations may set more, never fewer.
@ref law:7
GIVEN `hours a month she works` IS A NUMBER
      `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `paid hours for pregnancy check-ups under the Women's Work Law` `hours a month she works` `hours a month of a full position at her workplace` IS
    40 TIMES `the share of a position under section 7 of the Women's Work Law` `hours a month she works` `hours a month of a full position at her workplace`

#ASSERT `weeks of absence after a miscarriage under the Women's Work Law` 0 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `weeks of absence after a miscarriage under the Women's Work Law` 9 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `months of absence after the period on a doctor's word under the Women's Work Law` 8 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `works the position the parent's hour asks` 156 156
#ASSERT `works the position the parent's hour asks` 174 200
#ASSERT NOT `works the position the parent's hour asks` 150 156
