§§ `7א`

-- (א): the employer keeps paying for the weeks maternity pay was paid and
-- the weeks the pregnancy-protection benefit was paid, if contributions
-- were being paid (by both, or by the employer alone) and the employee paid
-- her own part for the period. (ב): only an employer the employee worked
-- for at least six months right before the pregnancy began; for the weeks
-- of maternity pay, also only if they were employed throughout the
-- pregnancy. (ג): the minister sets dates and rules for paying; no rule
-- here turns on them. A pension fund and a study fund are both provident
-- funds ("קופת גמל" as the provident-funds law defines it).
@ref law:7א
GIVEN `weeks maternity pay was paid` IS A NUMBER
      `weeks the pregnancy-protection benefit was paid` IS A NUMBER
      `contributions were being paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employed six months right before the pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employed throughout the pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks the employer keeps contributing` `weeks maternity pay was paid` `weeks the pregnancy-protection benefit was paid` `contributions were being paid` `employed six months right before the pregnancy` `employed throughout the pregnancy` IS
    IF `contributions were being paid` AND `employed six months right before the pregnancy`
    THEN `weeks the pregnancy-protection benefit was paid`
         PLUS (IF `employed throughout the pregnancy` THEN `weeks maternity pay was paid` ELSE 0)
    ELSE 0

#ASSERT `weeks the employer keeps contributing` 15 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `weeks the employer keeps contributing` 15 8 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 23
#ASSERT `weeks the employer keeps contributing` 15 8 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `weeks the employer keeps contributing` 15 8 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0

§§ `8`

-- An employer does not employ an employee, woman or man, he knows to be in
-- the birth and parenthood period. Time in weeks of the period.
@desc What the Women's Work Law forbids an employer, or has him do.
DECLARE `Women's Work Law act` IS ONE OF
    `employ the employee in the birth and parenthood period`
    `dismiss the employee or give notice for a date the law protects`
    `employ her overtime or on the weekly rest`

@ref law:8
GIVEN `weeks of the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Women's Work Law act`
DECIDE `no work in the birth and parenthood period` `weeks of the period` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `employ the employee in the birth and parenthood period`
    WITHIN `weeks of the period`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "Women's Work Law, section 8: no one is employed in the birth and parenthood period"

§§ `9`

-- (א): a pregnant employee not yet in the period, permanent, casual or
-- temporary, who worked six months for the employer or at the workplace, is
-- dismissed only with the Minister's permit, which he refuses where he
-- thinks the dismissal is connected to the pregnancy. (ב), (ב1): a
-- manpower contractor's temporary stop counts as a dismissal, and the
-- employer in fact may not cause one. (ג)(1): no dismissal, and no notice
-- for a date, in the period or in an absence under §7(ג)(2) or (ג2) — no
-- permit opens it. (1א): nor in the 60 days after it, but with the
-- Minister's permit, which he gives only where the dismissal is not
-- connected to the birth, the period or the absence AND the business has
-- stopped or the employer is bankrupt or wound up. (2): nor in an absence
-- under §7(ג)(1ג), (ד)(1) or (ד1), or the 60 days after it, but with the
-- Minister's permit, which he refuses where he thinks it connected. (2ג), a
-- temporary provision to 31.3.2027, leaves out of the 60 days an unpaid
-- leave in the determining period. (3): those periods do not count in the
-- days of notice. (ד): a woman in a shelter, in her absence and 150 days
-- after, only with a permit. (ה): one in fertility treatment, in the
-- absences of §7(ג)(4) or (ג1) and 150 days after them, only with a permit
-- the Minister refuses where he thinks it connected — towards two births at
-- most while with the same employer, and, where they had treatment towards
-- children with earlier spouses, towards two births with the present one
-- too; (2): not once two years have passed from the first such absence; (3)
-- the same without an absence, for 150 days from the start of treatment, on
-- notice and a doctor's confirmation. (ו): no dismissal, and no notice for
-- a date, in an absence after a miscarriage. (ז): a dismissal includes not
-- renewing a fixed-term contract of twelve months or more, or a shorter one
-- that renewed an employment right before it.
@desc A dismissal the Women's Work Law limits, as section 9 tells the cases apart.
DECLARE `case under section 9` IS ONE OF
    `pregnant, not yet in the period`
    `in the period or an absence under section 7(ג)(2) or (ג2)`
    `in the days after the period or that absence`
    `in an absence under section 7(ג)(1ג), (ד)(1) or (ד1), or the days after it`
    `in fertility treatment's absences, or the days after them`
    `in an absence after a miscarriage`
    `none of section 9's cases`

@ref law:9
`days after the period in which section 9 limits a dismissal` MEANS 60

`days after an absence under section 7(ד) in which section 9 limits a dismissal` MEANS 60

`days after fertility treatment's absences in which section 9 limits a dismissal` MEANS 150

`months with the employer before section 9(א) protects a pregnant employee` MEANS 6

-- Which case a dismissal falls in, by the days since the period, the
-- absence under §7(ד) or the fertility absences ended (a negative number
-- while it lasts).
@ref law:9
GIVEN `she is pregnant and not yet in the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days since the period ended` IS A NUMBER @desc negative while the period, or an absence under section 7(ג)(2), lasts; a large number if long past or none
      `days since the absence under section 7(ד) ended` IS A NUMBER @desc negative while it lasts; a large number if none
      `days since the fertility absences ended` IS A NUMBER @desc negative while they last; a large number if none
      `she is absent after a miscarriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `case under section 9`
DECIDE `the case under section 9` `she is pregnant and not yet in the period` `days since the period ended` `days since the absence under section 7(ד) ended` `days since the fertility absences ended` `she is absent after a miscarriage` IS
    BRANCH IF `she is absent after a miscarriage` THEN `in an absence after a miscarriage`
           IF `days since the period ended` LESS THAN 0 THEN `in the period or an absence under section 7(ג)(2) or (ג2)`
           IF `she is pregnant and not yet in the period` THEN `pregnant, not yet in the period`
           IF `days since the period ended` AT MOST `days after the period in which section 9 limits a dismissal`
           THEN `in the days after the period or that absence`
           IF `days since the absence under section 7(ד) ended` AT MOST `days after an absence under section 7(ד) in which section 9 limits a dismissal`
           THEN `in an absence under section 7(ג)(1ג), (ד)(1) or (ד1), or the days after it`
           IF `days since the fertility absences ended` AT MOST `days after fertility treatment's absences in which section 9 limits a dismissal`
           THEN `in fertility treatment's absences, or the days after them`
           OTHERWISE `none of section 9's cases`

-- Whether the Minister may permit the dismissal in a case: never in the
-- period or after a miscarriage; in the 60 days after the period only where
-- it is not connected and the business stopped (or bankruptcy or winding
-- up); in the other cases where he thinks it not connected.
GIVEN k IS A `case under section 9`
      `connected to the protected cause, in the Minister's view` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business stopped, or the employer is bankrupt or wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9 lets the Minister permit the dismissal` k `connected to the protected cause, in the Minister's view` `the business stopped, or the employer is bankrupt or wound up` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `in the period or an absence under section 7(ג)(2) or (ג2)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in an absence after a miscarriage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in the days after the period or that absence` THEN
        (NOT `connected to the protected cause, in the Minister's view`) AND `the business stopped, or the employer is bankrupt or wound up`
    WHEN `none of section 9's cases` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOT `connected to the protected cause, in the Minister's view`

-- A dismissal section 9 limits is barred unless the Minister permitted it,
-- and a permit is only what the Minister may give. Section 9(א) protects
-- after six months; 9(ה) towards the births it counts.
GIVEN k IS A `case under section 9`
      `months with the employer` IS A NUMBER
      `section 9(ה) covers the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9 limits the dismissal` k `months with the employer` `section 9(ה) covers the treatment` `the Minister permitted it` IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `none of section 9's cases` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `pregnant, not yet in the period` THEN
        `months with the employer` AT LEAST `months with the employer before section 9(א) protects a pregnant employee` AND (NOT `the Minister permitted it`)
    WHEN `in fertility treatment's absences, or the days after them` THEN
        `section 9(ה) covers the treatment` AND (NOT `the Minister permitted it`)
    WHEN `in the period or an absence under section 7(ג)(2) or (ג2)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in an absence after a miscarriage` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOT `the Minister permitted it`

-- (ה)(1)–(2): the fertility protection reaches treatment towards two births
-- at most while with this employer — and towards two births with the
-- present spouse where there was treatment towards children with earlier
-- spouses — and not once two years have passed from the first absence for
-- it with this employer. A birth here is one the treatment was towards.
GIVEN `births with this employer the treatment was towards before` IS A NUMBER
      `treated towards children with an earlier spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `births with the present spouse the treatment was towards before` IS A NUMBER
      `years since the first absence for it with this employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(ה) covers the treatment towards a birth` `births with this employer the treatment was towards before` `treated towards children with an earlier spouse` `births with the present spouse the treatment was towards before` `years since the first absence for it with this employer` IF
        (    `births with this employer the treatment was towards before` LESS THAN 2
         OR (`treated towards children with an earlier spouse` AND `births with the present spouse the treatment was towards before` LESS THAN 2))
    AND `years since the first absence for it with this employer` LESS THAN 2

-- And the rule itself: the employer does not dismiss, or give notice for a
-- date, where section 9 limits the dismissal.
GIVEN `section 9 limits it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Women's Work Law act`
DECIDE `no dismissal section 9 limits` `section 9 limits it` IS
    IF `section 9 limits it`
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         SHANT `dismiss the employee or give notice for a date the law protects`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "Women's Work Law, section 9: the dismissal is limited"
    ELSE FULFILLED

#ASSERT `the case under section 9` FALSE 30 9999 9999 FALSE EQUALS `in the days after the period or that absence`
#ASSERT `the case under section 9` FALSE 61 9999 9999 FALSE EQUALS `none of section 9's cases`
#ASSERT `the case under section 9` FALSE (-10) 9999 9999 FALSE EQUALS `in the period or an absence under section 7(ג)(2) or (ג2)`
#ASSERT `the case under section 9` FALSE 9999 9999 120 FALSE EQUALS `in fertility treatment's absences, or the days after them`
#ASSERT `section 9 limits the dismissal` `in the period or an absence under section 7(ג)(2) or (ג2)` 24 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 9 lets the Minister permit the dismissal` `in the days after the period or that absence` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 9 lets the Minister permit the dismissal` `in the days after the period or that absence` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `section 9(ה) covers the treatment towards a birth` 0 FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(ה) covers the treatment towards a birth` 2 FALSE 2 1
#ASSERT `section 9(ה) covers the treatment towards a birth` 2 TRUE 0 1
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(ה) covers the treatment towards a birth` 0 FALSE 0 2

§§ `10`

-- (א): from the fifth month of pregnancy, once she has told the employer
-- (or he learned of it), he does not employ her overtime or on the weekly
-- rest, even where the Hours of Work and Rest Law would let him; nor at
-- night, if she told him in writing she does not agree. (ב): he may, where
-- she agreed in writing and gave a gynaecologist's certificate that
-- nothing prevents it, on its terms. (ג): for four months from the end of
-- the period, no night work and no work on the weekly rest without her
-- written consent (but for the workplaces and jobs the regulations under
-- §2(ג) set). (ד): night work is work of which two hours at least fall
-- between 22:00 and 06:00.
@ref law:10
GIVEN `month of the pregnancy` IS A NUMBER
      `the employer knows of the pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she agreed in writing, on a gynaecologist's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 10 lets her be employed overtime or on the weekly rest` `month of the pregnancy` `the employer knows of the pregnancy` `she agreed in writing, on a gynaecologist's certificate` IF
        `month of the pregnancy` LESS THAN 5
    OR  NOT `the employer knows of the pregnancy`
    OR  `she agreed in writing, on a gynaecologist's certificate`

GIVEN `allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Women's Work Law act`
DECIDE `no overtime in pregnancy without her consent` `allowed` IS
    IF `allowed`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         SHANT `employ her overtime or on the weekly rest`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "Women's Work Law, section 10: no overtime or weekly-rest work from the fifth month"

`months after the period with no night work without her consent` MEANS 4

GIVEN `hours of the work between 22:00 and 06:00` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `night work under section 10(ד)` `hours of the work between 22:00 and 06:00` IF
    `hours of the work between 22:00 and 06:00` AT LEAST 2

#ASSERT NOT `section 10 lets her be employed overtime or on the weekly rest` 5 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 10 lets her be employed overtime or on the weekly rest` 4 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 10 lets her be employed overtime or on the weekly rest` 6 TRUE TRUE

§§ `19`

-- For this law, a State employee is like any other employee: it binds the
-- State as employer, and so the Ministry of Education towards the teachers
-- it employs.
@ref law:19
`the Women's Work Law binds the State as an employer` MEANS TRUE

§§ `23`

-- The law takes away no right an employee has by law, collective
-- agreement, contract of employment or custom: what an instrument gives
-- beyond it stands. For a right measured in one number, the employee has
-- the larger.
@ref law:23
GIVEN `what the law gives` IS A NUMBER, `what the instrument gives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what stands under section 23 of the Women's Work Law` `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives` IS
    max `what the law gives` `what the instrument gives`

#ASSERT `what stands under section 23 of the Women's Work Law` 4 12 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `what stands under section 23 of the Women's Work Law` 26 14 EQUALS 26
